format session-log-v1
stamp 20260819.221729
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan taper -- a line only ever shrinks, and the door widens the moment the work narrows
prompt Keaton set the loop running: be Kyri in Radiant Style, read the living card and the itineraries, close open agent-closable reds first, then take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first and send it as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. Every living row in crux/REDS.md carries a closure -- 80 closed by the count guard, 83 by the living-card ASCII witness, 84 on measurement 20260819.145920, 85 reopened and closed 20260819.134229 with a real loom, 81 82 86 87 all released. Nothing agent-closable stood open, so the line was clear for constructive work.
think The running thread named its own next rung. The newest log's recommend field, the unhand banner, and the unhand witness all say the same sentence: a run weighs a child by the line it was handed at spawn, and that line never moves while the child runs -- whether a child may give back an arc it has finished with is the next question. Lindy-first crux-first pointed straight at it: the Microkernel Target is the seated Lindy-priority double-seat, and this is its next tractable move.
think The name came from the Comlink tendency -- clear, fun, safe. A line that tapers as the work narrows says the whole idea in one warm word, and grep found no module wearing it (lotus carries taps and multitap, a different word).
think The hard question was how a run learns of a handback honestly. A declared schedule would be a fiction the supervisor cannot verify, and guessing would weigh a door against work still in flight. The answer already stood in the arc: notify.rye provisions a bell file per declared channel, so a note file per child is the same shape one tier up -- the supervisor-to-child notification a microkernel already gives a parent and its protection domain.
think The shape of a handback fell out of the walk. cycle.do_stand reads its arcs in the order the plan names them, so at every instant the child holds a suffix of its line -- and a suffix is one number. That made the whole memory a single byte per child, monotone by construction on the publishing side, and it made TaperReversed and TaperEmptied honest refusals about direction and floor rather than bookkeeping.
think Determinism was the real risk in a witness that spawns real processes. A one-way note would have made the measured claim a race. The two-way handshake fixes it: the child publishes and then waits, bounded, for the run to acknowledge, so the supervisor is guaranteed to hear before it reaps -- and both bounds mean neither side can ever hang the run. Three consecutive runs printed identical numbers.
think The first plan draft measured nothing. Two of its phases named menu rather than board, so the blocked head passed over to them and the held room filled to three exactly as the tapered room did. Rewriting every reader to name board is what made the two rooms genuinely disagree, and it is the same lesson this arc keeps teaching: a measurement is only honest when the shape it runs on can actually distinguish the two answers.
think The listen condition wanted care too. Firing only when a fill admitted nothing meant the very first fill -- which admits the standing child -- skipped the listen and went straight to a blocking reap. Widening it to any blocked moment with slots free and work waiting is both correct and the honest place to pay: a run trades a bounded look for the chance to spend a slot that would otherwise idle, and the banner names that trade rather than hiding it.
think A redundant guard surfaced while proving the RED paths. taper_refusal restated the floor that taper_line already derives, so deleting it changed nothing on metal -- a check that cannot fail is dead weight. Removing it left one floor, derived, and the RED path then showed as a real panic on the invariant that a narrowed line always keeps the arc its child is working.
think The council rota read this lap was item 23, the one-clock naming law. Its two tiers -- living names unstamped, dated artifacts stamped -- are exactly what this round leaned on: a stamped log and cairn beside living REMEMBER, README, and CAIRNS that move forward in place.
obs Five RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN was claimed: the direction refusal dropped and a line grows back an arc already given away; the floor loosened and the walk panics at reached unreachable; the reach refusal broken and a line naming an unhanded arc reads as within; the door answered by the line handed in both runs and the finding shows as the failure the narrower room bought no room at all, 2 against 2; the listen removed entirely and the run reports it heard no handback at all.
obs The narrower room is never less safe, only sometimes wider. Silence leaves every line at full width, which is precisely the held reading -- so a run that hears nothing reads as the rung below, all 9 pairs. That is the generalization test this arc runs every rung, and it is what makes the new room a strict widening rather than a gamble.
obs The Caravan README module table had drifted nine rungs behind the arc -- precede through unhand were prose sections with no row. Brought level in the same round under the ratchet-on-touch habit, since the file was already open for the taper section.
loom witness=caravan_taper_witness rungs=42 children=5 peak_handed=2 peak_taper=3 slots_handed=8 slots_taper=4 handbacks=2 pairs=9 wall_s=6
file caravan/taper.rye the rung -- a line that only shrinks, three refusals about direction floor and reach, the two-way note, and the supervisor that narrows its memory between fills
file tools/caravan_taper_witness.rish the witness -- native contains checks over the selftest, the five RED paths named in its head, GREEN on metal
file caravan/README.md the taper section, the nine missing table rows, and the unhand limit repointed at the rung that answers it
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moved to taper, the unhand chronicle folded into the prior-edges pointer, the git nib carried in the same commit
file crux/CAIRNS.md the walk-back row for that condensation, recorded before the card was swept
recommend keep-going the next rung's question is already named and is the mirror of this one -- whether a supervisor may hand a running child a wider line, work arriving for a child already in flight rather than leaving it. Mechanical, single-module, and the arc's own habit answers how to shape it: a widening must be refused wherever the ceiling would refuse it, which is the one place a shrink never had to look.
